<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The Android launch window, i.e. what is on screen between the launcher tap and Flutter's
  first frame (and, on Android 12+, the colour of the system splash — see values-v31/).

  IT IS A SINGLE COLOUR ON PURPOSE, AND THAT COLOUR IS THE LAUNCH GROUND, @color/splash_ground:
  the warm beige the Apnivaas launch animation is drawn on, measured off the shipped WebP. The
  Flutter splash paints the same value first and the animation's opening quarter-second is
  empty ground, so the window, the system splash and the first frame meet without a seam.

  A <color> root rather than a <layer-list> also matters on Android 12+, where the system
  splash screen adopts windowBackground only when it is a single colour (values-v31 sets
  windowSplashScreenBackground explicitly as well, so the two cannot drift).

  The drawable-night/ copy is identical: main.dart pins the app to its light theme, so a phone
  in dark mode still launches into the same beige.
-->
<color xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:color="@color/splash_ground" />
